# said -- words said another way aloud, for voice: a word a voice can't
# read as it is written, such as a name with no vowels, which it guesses
# at (a Hebrew voice said "יהוה" as "yo"). See "Voice" in
# readme.architecture.
#
# One word to a line: the word as the text has it, "=", then what to say.
# Only whole words are changed, not one inside a longer word. A word with
# vowel points, or with a letter joined to its front, is another word, and
# needs a line of its own.
#
# Only what is heard changes: the EBaC integration's voice ("EBaC voice",
# chosen in an Assist voice setup) puts these in place on the way to the
# speaker. The screen, the text Assist shows, and searching all keep the
# word as the text has it.

יהוה = Adonai
